        "text": "The first part, ∃x (P(x) ∧ E(x)), is the existence part: there is at least one number that is both prime and even. The second part, ∀y (P(y) ∧ E(y) → y = x), is the uniqueness part: if there is any number that is both prime and even, then it must be exactly the number x we found in the first part."
      },
      {
        "label": "uncertainty-estimation",
        "text": "But hold on, in the domain of positive integers, is there such a number? Let me think."
