        "text": "Let me visualize the cube. Each edge is 4 units long, so each edge has 4 smaller cubes. The two at the ends are corners, so they have three red faces. The ones in the middle of each edge, which are the second and third cubes from each corner, should have exactly two red faces because only two of their faces are on the original cube's faces, right?"
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Yes, that makes sense. So, for each edge, there are 2 such cubes. Since there are 12 edges, 12 times 2 is 24. So, 24 smaller cubes have exactly two red faces."
      },
      {
        "label": "uncertainty-estimation",
        "text": "Wait, but let me think again. Is there another way to calculate this?"
      },
      {
