 26*(x_i - 2))\n\nSo, the cross product is:\n\n[ -130 + 4*(y_i - 2) ]i + [180 - 4*(x_i - 2) ]j + [36*(y_i - 2) - 26*(x_i - 2)]k\n\nThe magnitude squared is:\n\n[ (-130 + 4y_i - 8)^2 + (180 - 4x_i + 8)^2 + (36y_i - 72 - 26x_i + 52)^2 ]\n\nSimplify:\n\n= [ (-138 + 4y_i)^2 + (188 - 4x_i)^2 + (36y_i - 26x_i - 20)^2 ]\n\nSimilarly, the magnitude of AB is sqrt(1988) as before.\n\nSo, the distance from AB to (x_i, y_i, 0) is sqrt( [ (-138 + 4y_i)^2 + (188 - 4x_i)^2 + (36y_i - 26x_i - 20)^2 ] ) / sqrt(1988)\n\nSimilarly, for point P2 = (x_i, y_i, 6):\n\nVector AP2 = (x_i - 2, y_i - 2, 1)\nCross product AB × AP2:\n\n|i     j     k|\n|36   26   -4|\n|x_i - 2   y_i - 2     1|\n\n= i*(26*1 - (-4)*(y_i - 2)) - j*(36*1 - (-4)*(x_i - 2)) + k*(36*(y_i - 2) - 26*(x_i - 2))\n\n= i*(26 + 4*(y_i - 2)) - j*(36 + 4*(x_i - 2)) + k*(36*(y_i - 2) - 26*(x_i - 2))\n\nSo, the cross product is:\n\n[26 + 4y_i - 8]i + [ -36 - 4x_i + 8 ]j + [36y_i - 72 - 26x_i + 52]k\n\nSimplify:\n\n= [18 + 4y_i]i + [ -28 - 4x_i ]j + [36y_i - 26x_i - 20]k\n\nMagnitude squared:\n\n[ (18 + 4y_i)^2 + (-28 - 4x_i)^2 + (36y_i - 26x_i - 20)^2 ]\n\nSo, the distance from AB to (x_i, y_i, 6) is sqrt( [ (18 + 4y_i)^2 + (-28 - 4x_i)^2 + (36y_i - 26x_i - 20)^2 ] ) / sqrt(1988)\n\nSo, for each column, we can compute these two distances and check if either is ≤0.5.\n\nAlternatively, since sqrt(1988) is a constant, we can compute the squared distances and compare with (0.5)^2 = 0.25.\n\nSo, for each column, compute the squared distance from AB to (x_i, y_i, 0) and (x_i, y_i, 6), and see if either is ≤0.25.\n\nLet me compute this for each column.\n\nFirst, Column 1: (10, 10)\n\nCompute distance to (10,10,0):\n\nCompute numerator squared:\n\n(-138 + 4*10)^2 + (188 - 4*10)^2 + (36*10 - 26*10 - 20)^2\n\n= (-138 + 40)^2 + (188 - 40)^2 + (360 - 260 - 20)^2\n\n= (-98)^2 + (148)^2 + (80)^2\n\n= 9604 + 21904 + 6400\n\n= 9604 + 21904 = 31508; 31508 + 6400 = 37908\n\nSo, squared distance is 37908 / 1988 ≈ 37908 / 1988 ≈ 19.05\n\nWhich is way larger than 0.25, so distance is sqrt(19.05) ≈ 4.36, which is way more than 0.5.\n\nSimilarly, distance to (10,10,6):\n\nCompute numerator squared:\n\n(18 + 4*10)^2 + (-28 - 4*10)^2 + (36*10 - 26*10 - 20)^2\n\n= (18 + 40)^2 + (-28 - 40)^2 + (360 - 260 - 20)^2\n\n= (58)^2 + (-68)^2 + (80)^2\n\n= 3364 + 4624 + 6400\n\n= 3364 + 4624 = 7988; 7988 + 6400 = 14388\n\nSquared distance: 14388 / 1988 ≈ 7.25\n\nAgain, way larger than 0.25.\n\nSo, Column 1: no intersection.\n\nColumn 2: (30, 10)\n\nCompute distance to (30,10,0):\n\nNumerator squared:\n\n(-138 + 4*10)^2 + (188 - 4*30)^2 + (36*10 - 26*10 - 20)^2\n\n= (-138 + 40)^2 + (188 - 120)^2 + (360 - 260 - 20)^2\n\n= (-98)^2 + (68)^2 + (80)^2\n\n= 9604 + 4624 + 6400\n\n= 9604 + 4624 = 14228; 14228 + 6400 = 20628\n\nSquared distance: 20628 / 1988 ≈ 10.38\n\nDistance ≈ 3.22, which is more than 0.5.\n\nDistance to (30,10,6):\n\nNumerator squared:\n\n(18 + 4*10)^2 + (-28 - 4*30)^2 + (36*10 - 26*10 - 20)^2\n\n= (18 + 40)^2 + (-28 - 120)^2 + (360 - 260 - 20)^2\n\n= (58)^2 + (-148)^2 + (80)^2\n\n= 3364 + 21904 + 6400\n\n= 3364 + 21904 = 25268; 25268 + 6400 = 31668\n\nSquared distance: 31668 / 1988 ≈ 15.94\n\nDistance ≈ 3.99, which is more than 0.5.\n\nSo, Column 2: no intersection.\n\nColumn 3: (20,15)\n\nCompute distance to (20,15,0):\n\nNumerator squared:\n\n(-138 + 4*15)^2 + (188 - 4*20)^2 + (36*15 - 26*15 - 20)^2\n\n= (-138 + 60)^2 + (188 - 80)^2 + (540 - 390 - 20)^2\n\n= (-78)^2 + (108)^2 + (130)^2\n\n= 6084 + 11664 + 16900\n\n= 6084 + 11664 = 17748; 17748 + 16900 = 34648\n\nSquared distance: 34648 / 1988 ≈ 17.44\n\nDistance ≈ 4.18, which is more than 0.5.\n\nDistance to (20,15,6):\n\nNumerator squared:\n\n(18 + 4*15)^2 + (-28 - 4*20)^2 + (36*15 - 26*15 - 20)^2\n\n= (18 + 60)^2 + (-28 - 80)^2 + (540 - 390 - 20)^2\n\n= (78)^2 + (-108)^2 + (130)^2\n\n= 6084 + 11664 + 16900\n\nSame as before: 6084 + 11664 = 17748; 17748 + 16900 = 34648\n\nSquared distance: 34648 / 1988 ≈ 17.44\n\nDistance ≈ 4.18, which is more than 0.5.\n\nSo,